    "description": "Birthdays are given as a tuple of (month, day) string pairs, e.g. (('May', '15'), ('June', '17')). Write three functions: unique_day(day, possible_birthdays) returns True if exactly one birthday has that day; unique_month(month, possible_birthdays) returns True if exactly one birthday has that month; contains_unique_day(month, possible_birthdays) returns True if that month has at least one birthday whose day is unique.",
    "global_code": "\n\ntuple_of_possible_birthdays = (('May', '15'),\n                              ('May', '16'),\n                              ('May', '19'),\n                              ('June', '17'),\n                              ('June', '18'),\n                              ('July', '14'),\n                              ('July', '16'),\n                              ('August', '14'),\n                              ('August', '15'),\n                              ('August', '17'))\n\n",
    "tests": [
      {
        "input": "unique_day(\"1\", ((\"January\",\"1\"),(\"February\",\"1\")))",
